<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Chagatai Khanate</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Chagatai Empire, Chagataid, Chagataids</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Chagatai Khanate was the Mongol successor state in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-asia">Central Asia</a> ruled by the descendants of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chagatai-khan">Chagatai Khan</a> from the thirteenth century. It covered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/transoxiana">Transoxiana</a> and the lands east to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tarim-basin">Tarim Basin</a> and gradually adopted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a>. Its western part later fell under the control of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timur">Timur</a>, founder of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timurid-empire">Timurid Empire</a>, while Chagatai khans continued to rule in the east.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/chagatai-khanate.jpg" alt="Chagatai Khanate" width="320" height="255" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: MapMaster · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Chagatai_Khanate_map_en.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
